IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-duties`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the worker (s 7) -- the baseline's seat, whose 36 questions are asked here by calling the baseline's functions in
--     whs-duties.l4;
--   * the person who runs a business or undertaking (a PCBU, s 5) -- the duty holder of ss 19-21, 38, 39, 47 and 273,
--     and the person who may not discriminate against a worker for raising a safety issue (s 104);
--   * a director or other officer of the business or undertaking (s 4A) -- bound by the due diligence duty of s 27 and
--     the officer's penalties of ss 30A(3), 31(2), 32 and 33.
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The regulator, an
-- inspector, a health and safety representative acting as such, a court and the Tribunal are never seats: what they may
-- or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * for the worker: `I live in accommodation that a business I work for owns, manages or controls` (s 19(4));
--     `an incident has happened at my work` (s 30 serious harm and the notifiable incident questions of ss 35-39);
--     `I have ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85` (ss 86, 88); and `what was done to me`
--     (an enumeration; `none of these` gives `does not arise for you` for the six questions of ss 104-115);
--   * for the business: `a worker of mine lives in accommodation I own, manage or control` (s 19(4)); `an incident has
--     happened at work in my business or undertaking` (ss 35-39); `a worker of mine has ceased, or refused to carry out,
--     work under section 84 or 85` (ss 86, 88); and `what I did, or would do, to the worker` (an enumeration; `none of
--     these` gives `does not arise for you` for the three questions of ss 104-110);
--   * the officer has none: every officer question arises for every officer.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (who is a worker, who owes a duty, what the duty requires, the
-- penalties for failing in a duty, the right to stop work) takes no situation input. The two helpers that read the
-- enumerated situations list every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's records (`The other person`, `Control of the
-- place`, `My injury or illness`) are taken as the baseline takes them; the business's own s 5 position is built here
-- from plain answers.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I work for a business or undertaking`
    `I run a business or undertaking`
    `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `imprisonment for` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Hours` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within` HAS `hours` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `keep it until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Next step` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `next step` HAS `the step` IS A `Control step`

-- The business's situation for ss 104-110, from its own side; each value is the s 105 conduct of the baseline's
-- `What was done to me`, and `none of these` gives `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `What I did to the worker` IS ONE OF
    `dismiss the worker`
    `terminate the worker's contract for services`
    `put the worker to their detriment in their engagement`
    `alter the worker's position to their detriment`
    `refuse or fail to offer to engage a prospective worker`
    `treat a prospective worker less favourably than others`
    `terminate a commercial arrangement with the person`
    `refuse or fail to enter into a commercial arrangement with the person`
    `threaten or organise one of these`
    `none of these`

-- The s 106 reasons, from the business's side.
DECLARE `Why I did it` IS ONE OF
    `the worker is, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member`
    `the worker took on another role under the Act`
    `the worker exercised, performed or refrained from a power or function under the Act`
    `the worker assisted or informed a person exercising a power under the Act`
    `the worker raised or proposed to raise a work health or safety issue or concern`
    `the worker was involved in resolving a work health and safety issue`
    `the worker took action to seek compliance with a duty under the Act`
    `for none of the prohibited reasons`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the new seats need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The worker's situation for ss 104-115: something in s 105 was done to me. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What was done to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `something was done to me` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `I was dismissed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my contract for services was terminated` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I was put to my detriment in my engagement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my position was altered to my detriment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I was not offered engagement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I was offered less favourable terms than another prospective worker` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commercial arrangement with me was terminated` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commercial arrangement with me was refused` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `one of these was threatened or organised` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

-- The business's situation for ss 104-110. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I did to the worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I did, or would do, something to the worker` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `dismiss the worker` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `terminate the worker's contract for services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `put the worker to their detriment in their engagement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `alter the worker's position to their detriment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refuse or fail to offer to engage a prospective worker` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `treat a prospective worker less favourably than others` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `terminate a commercial arrangement with the person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refuse or fail to enter into a commercial arrangement with the person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `threaten or organise one of these` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

-- The business's conduct as the baseline's s 105 conduct, value for value.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I did to the worker`
GIVETH A `What was done to me`
`what it is to the worker` `what` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `dismiss the worker` THEN `I was dismissed`
    WHEN `terminate the worker's contract for services` THEN `my contract for services was terminated`
    WHEN `put the worker to their detriment in their engagement` THEN `I was put to my detriment in my engagement`
    WHEN `alter the worker's position to their detriment` THEN `my position was altered to my detriment`
    WHEN `refuse or fail to offer to engage a prospective worker` THEN `I was not offered engagement`
    WHEN `treat a prospective worker less favourably than others` THEN `I was offered less favourable terms than another prospective worker`
    WHEN `terminate a commercial arrangement with the person` THEN `a commercial arrangement with me was terminated`
    WHEN `refuse or fail to enter into a commercial arrangement with the person` THEN `a commercial arrangement with me was refused`
    WHEN `threaten or organise one of these` THEN `one of these was threatened or organised`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN `none of these`

-- The business's reason as the baseline's s 106 reason, value for value.
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why I did it`
GIVETH A `Why it was done`
`the reason, as the Act puts it` `why` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `the worker is, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member` THEN `I am, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member`
    WHEN `the worker took on another role under the Act` THEN `I took on another role under the Act`
    WHEN `the worker exercised, performed or refrained from a power or function under the Act` THEN `I exercised, performed or refrained from a power or function under the Act`
    WHEN `the worker assisted or informed a person exercising a power under the Act` THEN `I assisted or informed a person exercising a power under the Act`
    WHEN `the worker raised or proposed to raise a work health or safety issue or concern` THEN `I raised or proposed to raise a work health or safety issue or concern`
    WHEN `the worker was involved in resolving a work health and safety issue` THEN `I was involved in resolving a work health and safety issue`
    WHEN `the worker took action to seek compliance with a duty under the Act` THEN `I took action to seek compliance with a duty under the Act`
    WHEN `for none of the prohibited reasons` THEN `for none of the prohibited reasons`

-- The person asking, as the baseline's `The other person`, when they say whether they conduct a business or
-- undertaking: the s 5 exclusions are folded into that one answer.
GIVEN `I conduct it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The other person`
`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct it` MEANS
    `The other person` WITH
        `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS `I conduct it`
        `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer`                  IS FALSE
        `is a local government member`                                                   IS FALSE
        `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes`               IS FALSE
        `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group`         IS FALSE

-- The person asking, as the baseline's `The other person`, from their s 5 answers.
GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      `d` IS A BOOLEAN
      `e` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The other person`
`me, from my answers` `a` `b` `c` `d` `e` MEANS
    `The other person` WITH
        `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS `a`
        `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer`                  IS `b`
        `is a local government member`                                                   IS `c`
        `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes`               IS `d`
        `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group`         IS `e`

-- The business as a duty holder for ss 30A-33: an individual conducting it, or a body corporate.
GIVEN `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty holder`
`me, as a duty holder` `I am a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `I am a body corporate` THEN `a body corporate` ELSE `an individual conducting the business or undertaking`

-- The Act's two-tier penalties: "(a) for an individual, a fine of ...; (b) for a body corporate, a fine of ...".
-- Used for s 47(1) ($25 000 / $115 000), s 38(7) ($5 500 / $30 000), s 39(1) ($12 500 / $55 000) and s 273
-- ($5 500 / $30 000), each read from the deposited text.
GIVEN `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for an individual` IS A NUMBER
      `for a body corporate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fine for an individual or a body corporate` `I am a body corporate` `for an individual` `for a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `I am a body corporate` THEN `for a body corporate` ELSE `for an individual`

§§ `For the worker (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (whs-duties.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 5, 7, 8 -- worker, business or undertaking, workplace`

@export Am I a worker under the Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) (s 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I carry out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do work, as an employee, contractor, employee of a contractor, labour hire worker, outworker, apprentice, trainee, work experience student, volunteer or otherwise, for a business or undertaking
      `I am an individual conducting the business and I carry out work in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you run the business yourself and also work in it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a worker under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a worker` `I carry out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or undertaking` `I am an individual conducting the business and I carry out work in it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this person conduct a business or undertaking (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this person run a business or undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person conduct a business or undertaking` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is this place a workplace (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `work is carried out there for a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether work is done at the place for a business
      `a worker goes there, or is likely to be there, while at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or another worker go to the place, or are likely to be there, while working
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this place a workplace under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Is this place a workplace` `work is carried out there for a business or undertaking` `a worker goes there, or is likely to be there, while at work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19-21 -- who owes me a duty of care`

@export Does this person owe me the primary duty of care (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
      `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker (s 7)
      `the person engaged me, or caused me to be engaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person employed or contracted you, or caused you to be engaged (for example by contracting your employer to supply you)
      `the person influences or directs my activities in carrying out work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person directs or influences how you do your work
      `I was at work in its business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were at work in that person's business or undertaking at the time
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this person owe me the primary duty of care under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the primary duty of care` `the person` `I am a worker` `the person engaged me, or caused me to be engaged` `the person influences or directs my activities in carrying out work` `I was at work in its business or undertaking`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this person ensure its work does not put my health and safety at risk (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
      `its work could put my health or safety at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether work done as part of that person's business could put you at risk
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this person make sure its work does not put me at risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must this person ensure its work does not put me at risk` `the person` `its work could put my health or safety at risk`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Asked only of a worker who lives in accommodation the business owns, manages or controls, so the s 19(4)(a) fact is
-- TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export Must my employer maintain the accommodation I live in for work (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I live in accommodation that a business I work for owns, manages or controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in accommodation that the business you work for owns, or manages or controls (s 19(4) arises only then)
      `I must live there for my engagement because other accommodation is not reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether living there is necessary for your work because nothing else is reasonably available
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my employer maintain the accommodation I live in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I live in accommodation that a business I work for owns, manages or controls`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must my employer maintain my accommodation` TRUE `I must live there for my engagement because other accommodation is not reasonably available`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this person, as a person with management or control of my workplace, keep it and its ways in and out without risk to me (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
      `control` IS A `Control of the place` @desc What part, if any, the person has in managing or controlling the place
      `the place is a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is a workplace (s 8)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this person owe me the duty of the person with management or control of my workplace` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the workplace duty` `the person` `control` `the place is a workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this person keep the fixtures, fittings or plant it manages or controls at my workplace without risk to me (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
      `control of the fixtures` IS A `Control of the place` @desc What part, if any, the person has in managing or controlling the fixtures, fittings or plant (the handrail, the lighting, the lift)
      `the place is a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is a workplace (s 8)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this person owe me the duty for the fixtures, fittings and plant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the fixtures duty` `the person` `control of the fixtures` `the place is a workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 17, regs 35, 36 -- what the duty requires`

@export What must the person who owes me the duty do next about this risk (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 17; regs 35, 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `eliminating the risk is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk could reasonably be removed altogether (for a wet stair: fixing the leak, or closing the stair)
      `a substitution, isolation or engineering control is reasonably practicable and not in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such a control (a non-slip surface, a drain, a barrier) could reasonably be added and is not there
      `an administrative control is reasonably practicable and not in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rule or procedure (warning signs, a cleaning roster, a changed patrol route) could reasonably be added and is not there
      `personal protective equipment is reasonably practicable and not provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether suitable protective equipment (slip-resistant footwear) could reasonably be provided and is not
GIVETH A `Next step`
`What must be done next about this risk to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `next step` (`What must be done next about this risk` `eliminating the risk is reasonably practicable` `a substitution, isolation or engineering control is reasonably practicable and not in place` `an administrative control is reasonably practicable and not in place` `personal protective equipment is reasonably practicable and not provided`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4A, 27, 28, 29 -- officers, me, and others at the workplace`

@export Must this officer exercise due diligence to see that the business meets its duty to me (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 4A, s 27(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `status` IS AN `Officer status` @desc What position the person holds in the business that owes you a duty
      `the business owes me a duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business the person is an officer of owes you a duty or obligation under the Act
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this officer exercise due diligence for the business's duty to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must this officer exercise due diligence for me` `status` `the business owes me a duty under the Act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I comply with this instruction from the business (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 28(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are at work
      `the business gave the instruction to allow it to comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business gave the instruction so that it can meet its duties under the Act
      `the instruction is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the instruction is a reasonable one
      `I am reasonably able to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are reasonably able to comply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I comply with this instruction from the business` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must I comply with this instruction` `I am at work` `the business gave the instruction to allow it to comply with the Act` `the instruction is reasonable` `I am reasonably able to comply`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this other person at my workplace take reasonable care not to affect my health and safety (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 29)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person is at a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is at the workplace
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this other person at my workplace take reasonable care for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must this person at the workplace take reasonable care for me` `the person is at a workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30-33 -- what the person who failed me can be made to pay`

@export Is my injury serious harm (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 30, s 31(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `it endangered, or was likely to endanger, my life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury or illness put your life in danger, or was likely to
      `it results, or is likely to result, in permanent injury or harm to my health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it leaves, or is likely to leave, a permanent injury or harm to your health
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my injury serious harm under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my injury serious harm` `it endangered, or was likely to endanger, my life` `it results, or is likely to result, in permanent injury or harm to my health`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most this duty holder can be fined for failing in its health and safety duty (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A-33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who` IS A `Duty holder` @desc Who failed in the duty: an individual running the business, an officer, another individual such as a worker (including you), or a company
      `outcome` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `knowing death or serious harm was likely, and in disregard of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the duty holder who failed me can be fined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `amount` (`What is the most the duty holder can be fined` `who` `outcome` `knowing death or serious harm was likely, and in disregard of it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, this duty holder faces for failing in its duty (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A, 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who` IS A `Duty holder` @desc Who failed in the duty: an individual running the business, an officer, another individual such as a worker (including you), or a company
      `outcome` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `knowing death or serious harm was likely, and in disregard of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH A `Years`
`What is the longest the duty holder who failed me can be imprisoned` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `imprisonment for` (`What is the longest prison term in years` `who` `outcome` `knowing death or serious harm was likely, and in disregard of it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35-39, reg 699 -- notifiable incidents`

@export Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 36; reg 699)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `mine` IS A `My injury or illness` @desc What your injury or illness required, and what a doctor thinks of it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my injury or illness serious` `mine`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was this a dangerous incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `it exposed a person to a serious risk to health or safety at a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident exposed you or anyone to a serious risk to health or safety, in relation to a workplace
      `the exposure was immediate or imminent, to` IS AN `Exposure` @desc What the immediate or imminent exposure was to
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was what happened a dangerous incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was this a dangerous incident` `it exposed a person to a serious risk to health or safety at a workplace` `the exposure was immediate or imminent, to`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is what happened a notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 35)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `a person died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person died
      `a person suffered a serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a serious injury or illness (s 36)
      `it was a dangerous incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a dangerous incident (s 37)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what happened a notifiable incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it a notifiable incident` `a person died` `a person suffered a serious injury or illness` `it was a dangerous incident`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must this business notify the regulator, immediately, of what happened to me (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `the person` IS A `The other person` @desc The business or person whose duty you are asking about: your employer, the building's manager, a tenant, a contractor
      `it is a notifiable incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened is a notifiable incident (s 35)
      `it arose out of the conduct of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident arose out of the conduct of that person's business or undertaking
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this business notify the regulator of what happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must this business notify the regulator` `the person` `it is a notifiable incident` `it arose out of the conduct of that business`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a business can be fined for not notifying the regulator of a notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `the business is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business is a company or other body corporate
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the business can be fined for not notifying the regulator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most it can be fined for not notifying` `the business is a body corporate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Until what date must the business keep its record of the notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `the day notice was given to the regulator` IS A DATE @desc The day the business notified the regulator
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`Until what date must the business keep its record of the incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `keep it until` (`Until when must the record be kept` `the day notice was given to the regulator`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the site of the incident be disturbed by this action (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 39)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at or arising out of your work that injured you or someone else, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on serious harm and notifiable incidents, ss 30, 35-39, arise only then)
      `an inspector has arrived, or the time an inspector directed has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inspector has arrived at the site, or any earlier time an inspector directed has come
      `the action` IS AN `Action at the site` @desc What is to be done at the site (mopping the stair, moving the injured person, clearing the area)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the site of the incident be disturbed by this action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at my work`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the site be disturbed` `an inspector has arrived, or the time an inspector directed has passed` `the action`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 47 -- consultation`

@export Must the business consult me about this health or safety matter (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 47(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I carry out work for the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do work for the business
      `I am, or am likely to be, directly affected by the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work health or safety matter affects you directly, or is likely to
      `consulting me is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably practicable to consult you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the business consult me about this health or safety matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must the business consult me` `I carry out work for the business` `I am, or am likely to be, directly affected by the matter` `consulting me is reasonably practicable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 84-88 -- stopping unsafe work`

@export May I cease, or refuse to carry out, this work (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 84)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker (s 7)
      `I reasonably fear a serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard, to me or someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable concern that doing the work would expose you, or another person, to a serious risk to health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard
      `I am a police officer and stopping would or could harm a covert or dangerous operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for police officers
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I stop or refuse this work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`May I cease or refuse this work` `I am a worker` `I reasonably fear a serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard, to me or someone else` `I am a police officer and stopping would or could harm a covert or dangerous operation`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my health and safety representative direct me to stop work (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 85)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am in the representative's work group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative represents your work group
      `the representative reasonably fears a serious risk to me from an immediate or imminent hazard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative has that reasonable concern about you
      `the representative consulted the business and tried to resolve the issue, without success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative first consulted the business and tried to resolve the matter as an issue
      `the risk is too serious and immediate to consult first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk is so serious and immediate or imminent that consulting first is not reasonable
      `the representative has completed the initial training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative has completed the prescribed initial training, or equivalent
      `the direction would or could harm a covert or dangerous operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for police work
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my health and safety representative direct me to stop this work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`May my representative direct me to stop work` `I am in the representative's work group` `the representative reasonably fears a serious risk to me from an immediate or imminent hazard` `the representative consulted the business and tried to resolve the issue, without success` `the risk is too serious and immediate to consult first` `the representative has completed the initial training` `the direction would or could harm a covert or dangerous operation`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Asked only of a worker who has stopped work under s 84 or 85, so the first fact of the baseline's s 86 question is
-- TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export Must I tell the business, as soon as practicable, that I have stopped work (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 86(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have stopped or refused work because of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard (s 84), or on your health and safety representative's direction (s 85)
      `I stopped on a representative's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you stopped because your health and safety representative directed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I tell the business that I have stopped work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I have ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I tell the business I have stopped` TRUE `I stopped on a representative's direction`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the continuity of my engagement protected after I stopped work (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 88)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have stopped or refused work because of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard (s 84), or on your health and safety representative's direction (s 85)
      `I unreasonably failed to do suitable, safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you unreasonably failed to follow a direction to do suitable alternative work that was safe and appropriate for you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my continuity of engagement protected after I stopped work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I have ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `I unreasonably failed to do suitable, safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 104-115 -- discrimination for raising a safety issue`

@export Was what was done to me discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 105, 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `why` IS A `Why it was done` @desc The reason it was done, or the reason alleged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was what was done to me discriminatory conduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was it discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `what was done to me` `why`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is what was done to me an offence under section 104 (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 104, 110)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `why` IS A `Why it was done` @desc The reason it was done, or the reason alleged
      `the accused proves the reason was not the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person accused proves, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not the dominant one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what was done to me an offence under section 104` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it a discrimination offence` `what was done to me` `why` `the accused proves the reason was not the dominant reason`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the person who engaged in discriminatory conduct against me can be fined (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 104)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is a company or other body corporate
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the person who discriminated against me can be fined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most they can be fined for discrimination` `the person is a body corporate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my application to the Tribunal within 1 year after I knew, or ought to have known, I had a cause of action (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 113(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `the day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that the cause of action accrued
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you commence the proceeding
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my application to the Tribunal in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my Tribunal application in time` `the day I knew or ought to have known` `the day I apply`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Tribunal make an order for me for discriminatory conduct (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 112, 113, 115)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `why` IS A `Why it was done` @desc The reason it was done, or the reason alleged
      `the defendant proves the reason was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you complain of proves, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not a substantial one
      `the defendant proves the conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person proves the s 113(3) defence
      `my application is in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply within 1 year (s 113(1))
      `other proceedings` IS AN `Another proceeding` @desc Whether you have brought, won compensation in, or lost, another proceeding on the same matter
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Tribunal make an order for me for what was done` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Tribunal make an order for me` `what was done to me` `why` `the defendant proves the reason was not a substantial reason` `the defendant proves the conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with the Act` `my application is in time` `other proceedings`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Tribunal order that I be reinstated or employed (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 112(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the business or person did to you, or threatened or organised against you (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `the Tribunal can make an order for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal can make an order for you (ss 112, 113, 115)
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were or are an employee, or applied to be one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Tribunal order that I be reinstated or employed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `something was done to me` `what was done to me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Tribunal order my reinstatement` `the Tribunal can make an order for me` `what was done to me` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 267, 272, 273 -- general rules`

@export Does this Act itself give me a right to sue for this contravention (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 267)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contravention is of Part 6 (discriminatory or coercive conduct)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complain of is discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct under Part 6
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this Act give me a right to sue for this contravention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does the Act give me a right to sue` `the contravention is of Part 6 (discriminatory or coercive conduct)`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this term of my contract have effect (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 272)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it, or transfers a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term tries to exclude, limit or change the Act or a duty owed under it, or to pass a duty to someone else
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this term of my contract have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this term have effect` `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it, or transfers a duty`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the business charge me for this (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 273)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a worker of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker of the business
      `the charge is for something done or provided in relation to work health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the levy or charge is for safety equipment, training or anything else done or provided for work health and safety
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the business charge me for this safety item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I work for a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`May the business charge me for this` `I am a worker of the business` `the charge is for something done or provided in relation to work health and safety`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person who runs the business or undertaking (ss 5, 17, 19-21, 30A-39, 47, 86, 88, 104, 272, 273)`

-- The person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU) owes the duties of ss 19-21, 38, 39, 47 and 273. Where a
-- duty turns on being a PCBU, the question asks `I conduct a business or undertaking` (s 5) rather than assuming it
-- from the role, and "Do I conduct a business or undertaking" works it out.

§§§ `s 5 -- do I conduct a business or undertaking`

@export Do I conduct a business or undertaking (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I carry on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, whether or not for profit or gain (s 5(1))
      `I am an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual who is engaged in the business only as a worker in it or an officer of it (s 5(4))
      `I am a local government member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a local government member (s 5(5))
      `we are a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a group of volunteers working together for one or more community purposes (s 5(10))
      `any of us volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the volunteers employs anyone to carry out work for the group (s 5(10))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I conduct a business or undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person conduct a business or undertaking` (`me, from my answers` `I carry on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` `I am an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` `I am a local government member` `we are a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` `any of us volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19-21 -- the duties I owe`

@export Do I owe this worker the primary duty of care (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I conduct a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct a business or undertaking (s 5): one you run alone or with others, for profit or not, and not only as a worker or officer in it, as a local government member, or as a volunteer association
      `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a worker (s 7): someone who carries out work in any capacity for your business or undertaking
      `I engaged the worker, or caused the worker to be engaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employed or contracted the worker, or caused them to be engaged (for example by contracting a labour hire or security company to supply them)
      `I influence or direct the worker's activities in carrying out work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you direct or influence how the worker does their work
      `the worker was at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was at work in your business or undertaking at the time
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I owe this worker the primary duty of care` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the primary duty of care` (`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct a business or undertaking`) `the person is a worker` `I engaged the worker, or caused the worker to be engaged` `I influence or direct the worker's activities in carrying out work` `the worker was at work in my business or undertaking`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I ensure that the work of my business does not put other people's health and safety at risk (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I conduct a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct a business or undertaking (s 5): one you run alone or with others, for profit or not, and not only as a worker or officer in it, as a local government member, or as a volunteer association
      `my work could put a person's health or safety at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether work done as part of your business or undertaking could put anyone's health or safety at risk: a visitor, a member of the public, another business's worker
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I make sure my work does not put other people at risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must this person ensure its work does not put me at risk` (`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct a business or undertaking`) `my work could put a person's health or safety at risk`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The s 19(4)(a) fact is TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export Must I maintain the accommodation my worker lives in so that the worker is not exposed to risks (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 19(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a worker of mine lives in accommodation I own, manage or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a worker of yours lives in accommodation that your business owns, or manages or controls (s 19(4) arises only then)
      `the worker must live there for the engagement because other accommodation is not reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether living there is necessary for the worker's engagement because other accommodation is not reasonably available
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I maintain the accommodation my worker lives in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `a worker of mine lives in accommodation I own, manage or control`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must my employer maintain my accommodation` TRUE `the worker must live there for the engagement because other accommodation is not reasonably available`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I, as a person with management or control of this workplace, keep it and its ways in and out without risk to anyone (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I conduct a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct a business or undertaking (s 5): one you run alone or with others, for profit or not, and not only as a worker or officer in it, as a local government member, or as a volunteer association
      `my control of the place` IS A `Control of the place` @desc What part, if any, your business has in managing or controlling the place, and whether it is a residence you occupy
      `the place is a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is a workplace (s 8)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I keep this workplace without risk, as the person with management or control of it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the workplace duty` (`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct a business or undertaking`) `my control of the place` `the place is a workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I keep the fixtures, fittings or plant I manage or control at this workplace without risk to anyone (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I conduct a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct a business or undertaking (s 5): one you run alone or with others, for profit or not, and not only as a worker or officer in it, as a local government member, or as a volunteer association
      `my control of the fixtures` IS A `Control of the place` @desc What part, if any, your business has in managing or controlling the fixtures, fittings or plant (the handrail, the lighting, the lift)
      `the place is a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is a workplace (s 8)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I keep the fixtures, fittings and plant I manage or control without risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this person owe me the fixtures duty` (`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct a business or undertaking`) `my control of the fixtures` `the place is a workplace`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 17, regs 35, 36 -- what the duty requires of me`

@export What must I do next about this risk (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 17; regs 35, 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `eliminating the risk is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk could reasonably be removed altogether (for a wet stair: fixing the leak, or closing the stair)
      `a substitution, isolation or engineering control is reasonably practicable and not in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such a control (a non-slip surface, a drain, a barrier) could reasonably be added and is not there
      `an administrative control is reasonably practicable and not in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rule or procedure (warning signs, a cleaning roster, a changed patrol route) could reasonably be added and is not there
      `personal protective equipment is reasonably practicable and not provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether suitable protective equipment (slip-resistant footwear) could reasonably be provided and is not
GIVETH A `Next step`
`What must I do next about this risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `next step` (`What must be done next about this risk` `eliminating the risk is reasonably practicable` `a substitution, isolation or engineering control is reasonably practicable and not in place` `an administrative control is reasonably practicable and not in place` `personal protective equipment is reasonably practicable and not provided`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 47 -- consulting my workers`

@export Must I consult this worker about this health or safety matter (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 47(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the worker carries out work for my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker carries out work for your business or undertaking
      `the worker is, or is likely to be, directly affected by the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work health or safety matter affects the worker directly, or is likely to
      `consulting the worker is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably practicable to consult the worker
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I consult this worker about this health or safety matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must the business consult me` `the worker carries out work for my business or undertaking` `the worker is, or is likely to be, directly affected by the matter` `consulting the worker is reasonably practicable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not consulting my workers (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 47(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not consulting my workers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `amount` (`the fine for an individual or a body corporate` `I am a body corporate` 25000 115000)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30A-33 -- what I can be made to pay`

@export What is the most I can be fined for failing in my health and safety duty as the person conducting the business or undertaking (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A, 31-33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
      `what my failure did` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for failing in my health and safety duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `amount` (`What is the most the duty holder can be fined` (`me, as a duty holder` `I am a body corporate`) `what my failure did` `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, I face for failing in my health and safety duty as the person conducting the business or undertaking (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A, 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
      `what my failure did` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH A `Years`
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for failing in my health and safety duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `imprisonment for` (`What is the longest prison term in years` (`me, as a duty holder` `I am a body corporate`) `what my failure did` `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35-39, reg 699 -- an incident in my business`

@export Is the injury or illness a serious injury or illness (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 36; reg 699)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `the injury or illness` IS A `My injury or illness` @desc What the injured or ill person's injury or illness required, and what a doctor thinks of it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the injury or illness a serious injury or illness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my injury or illness serious` `the injury or illness`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was the incident a dangerous incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `it exposed a person to a serious risk to health or safety at a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident exposed you or anyone to a serious risk to health or safety, in relation to a workplace
      `the exposure was immediate or imminent, to` IS AN `Exposure` @desc What the immediate or imminent exposure was to
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was it a dangerous incident in my business` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was this a dangerous incident` `it exposed a person to a serious risk to health or safety at a workplace` `the exposure was immediate or imminent, to`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is what happened a notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 35)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `a person died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person died
      `a person suffered a serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a serious injury or illness (s 36)
      `it was a dangerous incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a dangerous incident (s 37)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what happened in my business a notifiable incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it a notifiable incident` `a person died` `a person suffered a serious injury or illness` `it was a dangerous incident`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I notify the regulator, immediately, of the incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `I conduct a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct a business or undertaking (s 5): one you run alone or with others, for profit or not, and not only as a worker or officer in it, as a local government member, or as a volunteer association
      `it is a notifiable incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened is a notifiable incident (s 35)
      `it arose out of the conduct of my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident arose out of the conduct of your business or undertaking
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I notify the regulator of the incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must this business notify the regulator` (`me, if I conduct a business or undertaking` `I conduct a business or undertaking`) `it is a notifiable incident` `it arose out of the conduct of my business or undertaking`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not notifying the regulator of a notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not notifying the regulator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most it can be fined for not notifying` `I am a body corporate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I notified the regulator by telephone and it requires a written notice, within how many hours must I give it (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
GIVETH A `Hours`
`Within how many hours must I give the regulator a written notice once it requires one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `within` `hours to give a written notice once required`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Until what date must I keep my record of the notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `the day I notified the regulator` IS A DATE @desc The day you notified the regulator of the incident
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`Until what date must I keep my record of the incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `keep it until` (`Until when must the record be kept` `the day I notified the regulator`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not keeping a record of the notifiable incident for 5 years (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 38(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not keeping the record` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `amount` (`the fine for an individual or a body corporate` `I am a body corporate` 5500 30000)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I, as the person with management or control of the workplace, disturb the site of the incident by this action (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 39)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `an inspector has arrived, or the time an inspector directed has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inspector has arrived at the site, or any earlier time an inspector directed has come
      `the action` IS AN `Action at the site` @desc What is to be done at the site (mopping the stair, moving the injured person, clearing the area)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I disturb the site of the incident by this action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the site be disturbed` `an inspector has arrived, or the time an inspector directed has passed` `the action`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not preserving the site of a notifiable incident (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 39(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something has happened at work in your business or undertaking that injured someone, made someone ill, killed someone, or exposed someone to a serious risk to health or safety (the questions on notifiable incidents, ss 35-39, arise only then)
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for disturbing the site` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `an incident has happened at work in my business or undertaking`
        THEN `amount` (`the fine for an individual or a body corporate` `I am a body corporate` 12500 55000)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 86-88 -- a worker who stops work`

-- The first fact of the baseline's s 86 question is TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export Must the worker who stopped work tell me, as soon as practicable, that they have stopped (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 86(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a worker of mine has ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a worker of yours has stopped or refused work because of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard (s 84), or on a health and safety representative's direction (s 85)
      `the worker stopped on a representative's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker stopped because a health and safety representative directed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the worker tell me that they have stopped work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `a worker of mine has ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I tell the business I have stopped` TRUE `the worker stopped on a representative's direction`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the continuity of engagement of the worker who stopped work protected (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 87, 88)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a worker of mine has ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a worker of yours has stopped or refused work because of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard (s 84), or on a health and safety representative's direction (s 85)
      `the worker unreasonably failed to do suitable, safe and appropriate alternative work I directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker unreasonably failed to follow your direction to do suitable alternative work at the same or another workplace that was safe and appropriate for them (s 87)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the worker's continuity of engagement protected` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `a worker of mine has ceased, or refused to carry out, work under section 84 or 85`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `the worker unreasonably failed to do suitable, safe and appropriate alternative work I directed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 104-110 -- what I may not do to a worker who raises a safety issue`

@export Would what I did, or would do, to the worker be discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 105, 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did, or would do, to the worker` IS A `What I did to the worker` @desc What you did, or would do, to the worker or prospective worker, or threatened or organised (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `why I did it` IS A `Why I did it` @desc The reason you did it, or would do it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would this be discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I did, or would do, something to the worker` `what I did, or would do, to the worker`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was it discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` (`what it is to the worker` `what I did, or would do, to the worker`) (`the reason, as the Act puts it` `why I did it`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Would what I did, or would do, to the worker be an offence under section 104 (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 104, 110)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did, or would do, to the worker` IS A `What I did to the worker` @desc What you did, or would do, to the worker or prospective worker, or threatened or organised (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `why I did it` IS A `Why I did it` @desc The reason you did it, or would do it
      `I can prove the reason was not the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you could prove, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not the dominant one (s 110(2); for the court)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would this be an offence for me under section 104` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I did, or would do, something to the worker` `what I did, or would do, to the worker`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it a discrimination offence` (`what it is to the worker` `what I did, or would do, to the worker`) (`the reason, as the Act puts it` `why I did it`) `I can prove the reason was not the dominant reason`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 104(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did, or would do, to the worker` IS A `What I did to the worker` @desc What you did, or would do, to the worker or prospective worker, or threatened or organised (if none of these, the questions on discriminatory conduct do not arise)
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for discriminatory conduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `I did, or would do, something to the worker` `what I did, or would do, to the worker`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most they can be fined for discrimination` `I am a body corporate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 272, 273 -- contracts and charges`

@export May I charge my worker for this (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 273)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person is my worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a worker of your business or undertaking
      `the charge is for something done or provided in relation to work health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the levy or charge is for safety equipment, training or anything else done or provided for work health and safety
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I charge my worker for this` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`May the business charge me for this` `the person is my worker` `the charge is for something done or provided in relation to work health and safety`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for charging a worker for anything done or provided for work health and safety (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 273)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conduct the business or undertaking as a company or other body corporate, rather than as an individual
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for charging a worker for work health and safety` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `amount` (`the fine for an individual or a body corporate` `I am a body corporate` 5500 30000)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this term of my contract or agreement have effect (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 272)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it, or transfers a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term tries to exclude, limit or change the Act or a duty owed under it, or to pass a duty to someone else
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this term of my contract with a worker have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I run a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Does this term have effect` `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it, or transfers a duty`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a director or other officer of the business or undertaking (ss 4A, 27, 30A(3), 31-33)`

-- s 27(1) puts the officer's own duty of due diligence; ss 30A(3), 31(2), 32 and 33 set the officer's penalties. Every
-- question here arises for every officer, so none takes a situation input (D8).

§§§ `ss 4A, 27 -- am I an officer, and my duty of due diligence`

@export Am I an officer of the business or undertaking under the Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) (s 4A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my position` IS AN `Officer status` @desc What position you hold: a Corporations Act s 9 officer who is not a partner (a director or secretary, or someone who makes or takes part in making decisions that affect the whole or a substantial part of the business), an officer of the Crown or of a public corporation, the Governor, a Minister or a local government member acting as such, or none of these
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an officer under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`is an officer` `my position`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I exercise due diligence to ensure that the business or undertaking complies with its duty or obligation (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) s 27(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my position` IS AN `Officer status` @desc What position you hold: a Corporations Act s 9 officer who is not a partner (a director or secretary, or someone who makes or takes part in making decisions that affect the whole or a substantial part of the business), an officer of the Crown or of a public corporation, the Governor, a Minister or a local government member acting as such, or none of these
      `the business has a duty or obligation under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business or undertaking you are an officer of has a duty or obligation under the Act
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I exercise due diligence to see that the business complies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking` THEN `yes if` (`Must this officer exercise due diligence for me` `my position` `the business has a duty or obligation under the Act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30A(3), 31-33 -- what I can be made to pay`

@export What is the most I can be fined, as an officer, for failing in my duty (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A(3), 31(2), 32, 33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the failure did` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined, as an officer, for failing in my duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking` THEN `amount` (`What is the most the duty holder can be fined` `an individual who is an officer` `what the failure did` `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, I face as an officer for failing in my duty (Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) ss 30A(3), 31(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the failure did` IS A `What the failure did` @desc What the failure did: caused a death, caused serious harm, exposed someone to a risk, or none of these
      `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the court's finding, the conduct was engaged in knowing it was likely to cause death or serious harm and in disregard of that (only matters for a death)
GIVETH A `Years`
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned, as an officer, for failing in my duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking` THEN `imprisonment for` (`What is the longest prison term in years` `an individual who is an officer` `what the failure did` `I knew death or serious harm was likely, and disregarded it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
